  "marked": false,
  "answer": "<p>The <b>correct</b> solution is to create a notification rule in CodeCommit that sends pull request events directly to the AWS Chatbot client integrated with your Slack workspace (Option 1 above). This enables the notification to be delivered straight to Slack via AWS Chatbot, utilizing the built-in integration between CodeCommit and AWS Chatbot that supports direct notifications to chat applications.</p><p>Here's why the other options are <i>incorrect</i>:</p><ul><li><i>Within the AWS Chatbot console, create a rule that listens for CodeCommit pull request activity and tailor the notifications as needed.</i> — AWS Chatbot itself does not allow you to create notification rules for CodeCommit repositories. Notification rules are created in CodeCommit or via AWS CodeStar Notifications, with Chatbot being the target.</li><li><i>In CodeCommit, generate a notification rule for pull request actions and configure it to send events to an SNS topic tied to the AWS Chatbot's ARN.</i> — While SNS topics can be used, AWS Chatbot is directly supported as a target for CodeCommit notification rules. Sending notifications via SNS is unnecessary and adds complexity.</li><li><i>Set up an SNS topic, hook up CodeCommit's pull request events to it, and add the AWS Chatbot client as a direct subscriber to this topic.</i> — Similar to the previous option, this is not the recommended approach because notification rules in CodeCommit natively support AWS Chatbot as a target. SNS configuration is more manual and is only needed when direct integration isn’t available.</li></ul><p><b>Tip:</b> Always use direct integrations—like CodeCommit notifications to Chatbot—when available, as this streamlines configuration, reduces possible misrouting of events, and simplifies permissions management.</p>",
  "query": "<p>Your team recently set up an AWS Chatbot client that can send messages to your Slack workspace. Now that the group is using AWS CodeCommit for git repositories, you'd like users in Slack to be alerted whenever someone creates or merges a pull request in these repositories. What is the best way to ensure Slack receives timely notifications about these pull request events through the AWS Chatbot?</p>",
